  m_GameObject: {fileID: 801015218}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0b4476788ca923842ad27e9edc2705e1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  npcDialoguePanel: {fileID: 275839330}
  npcDialogueText: {fileID: 19559559}
  npcDialoguePanel2: {fileID: 1129616890}
  npcDialogueText2: {fileID: 1287806617}
  playerDialoguePanel: {fileID: 796309174}
  playerDialogueText: {fileID: 667546235}
  npcContButton: {fileID: 703037372}
  npcContButton2: {fileID: 926037980}
  playerContButton: {fileID: 778509701}
  dialogue:
  - speaker: Elana
    line: "Greetings, Mr. Jacob. I\u2019ve brought a guest who wishes to speak with
      you."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: Oh, Elana! A guest for me, you say?
  - speaker: Elana
    line: Yes, this is Hazil.
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "Pleasure to meet you, Mr. Jacob. I\u2019m Hazil."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: Welcome to the Hayes family mansion, Sir Hazil.
  - speaker: Elana
    line: "Hazil has some questions he\u2019d like to ask you, Mr. Jacob."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "Questions, you say? I\u2019m curious. What would you like to know?"
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "I\u2019ve noticed something strange. Why haven\u2019t I seen any other
      staff in this mansion? Elana mentioned this place requires a lot of people
      to maintain."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "Ah, that\u2019s simple. The staff are currently resting. It\u2019s not
      their working hours, and some of them are busy in another section of the hall.
      That\u2019s why you haven\u2019t seen many people around."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: I see. That explains it. Though, I did meet Elana... and a girl with long silver hair named
      Alice.
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "Alice? Hmm... I\u2019m not familiar with that name. A girl with long silver
      hair, you say? We have several staff with similar descriptions, but none named
      Alice, as far as I know."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "Oh, I see. So you\u2019re not aware of her. It\u2019s alright."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "About this room of antiques... The Hayes family seems to have a fondness
      for collecting them, don\u2019t they?"
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: Indeed. The Hayes family treasures these artifacts as a symbol of their
      pride and wealth.
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: Impressive. But I noticed two display cases are empty. What happened to
      those items?
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "Ah, yes. Two antiques went missing due to a management oversight. We\u2019ve
      been searching for them ever since."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: Missing? That sounds serious.
  - speaker: Elana
    line: Yes, everyone was in a panic when we discovered the items were gone.
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "The staff checked everything thoroughly, but during a large gathering
      in the mansion, the items vanished from the basement. With tight security during
      the event, it\u2019s a mystery how they disappeared."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: That truly is a mystery.
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "It has everyone baffled. We\u2019re still trying to figure out how it
      happened."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "One more question... I\u2019ve heard rumors that this mansion is haunted
      or abandoned because of the strange \"shadow\" entities. Is that true?"
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: No, this mansion is neither abandoned nor haunted. As you can see, people
      live and work here.
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "However, those \"shadows\" you mentioned appeared a few years after a
      major Hayes family gathering. We don\u2019t know why they appeared, but they
      despise light."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "They\u2019re extremely dangerous. If they catch you, you might not return
      alive. They tend to roam in dark areas, especially the basement where there\u2019s
      no light source."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "Why haven\u2019t you reported this to the police or some organization?"
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "To outsiders, such a report would seem ludicrous. It would damage the
      Hayes family\u2019s reputation, and few would believe such a story."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: ...You might have a point there.
  - speaker: Elana
    line: No wonder they chased us so quickly when we encountered them!
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "What? Elana, you encountered the shadows? I\u2019ve warned you not to
      wander around the mansion."
  - speaker: Elana
    line: " I\u2019m sorry, Mr. Jacob. I was searching for Milady, who went missing
      when I lost sight of her. That\u2019s when I ran into Hazil in the basement."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: '!!! Next time, report to me immediately if something like this happens.
      As a staff member, you should notify someone in charge rather than acting alone.'
  - speaker: Elana
    line: "Understood. But we hadn\u2019t found Milady yet..."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "There\u2019s no need to search for her any longer. I\u2019ve already found
      her and taken her to her room."
  - speaker: Elana
    line: What? Milady has been found?
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "That\u2019s great news, Elana! You must be relieved."
  - speaker: Elana
    line: Yes, my heart nearly stopped when she went missing.
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: Elana, you must focus on your duty. You need to take care of Milady now.
  - speaker: Elana
    line: But I promised Hazil I would help him search for Alice...
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "Indeed, but your primary duty is to care for Milady. Don\u2019t forget
      your responsibilities."
  - speaker: Elana
    line: "...I understand. I\u2019m sorry for overstepping."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "It\u2019s okay, Elana. I understand it can\u2019t be helped."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: One last question. How can I leave this mansion?
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: ??? Leave? Sir Hazil, you can simply use the front door or the back exit
      if you wish to go.
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "I see... This place is truly full of mysteries. Thank you for your time,
      Mr. Jacob. I\u2019ll continue my search."
  - speaker: Mr. Jacob
    line: "I hope you find what you\u2019re seeking, Sir Hazil. If you need any help,
      my door is always open."
  - speaker: Hazil
    line: "Thank you. I\u2019ll keep that in mind. Farewell, Elana, Mr. Jacob."
  - speaker: Elana
    line: Goodbye, Hazil. Stay safe.
  wordSpeed: 0.05
